 " Speculate about different people and situations from images.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 5, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "Healthy eating is very important. There are so many articles and conversations about it, that it must be difficult for a large number of people. Don't get schooled about eating your vegetables! Think about putting together your own healthy diet by following a few small, easy-to-manage steps, like the way you learn new things at school or work.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": ""}, {"text": "Start by preparing as many of your meals as possible and follow a schedule. Cut down on unhealthy foods, and replace them with more nutritious ones. Substituting\nvegetable fats (for example, switching butter for olive oil) for animal fats\nwill be beneficial to your health. I speculate that eating healthy must make a\ndifference in how you feel.", "id": 2, "time": "17500", "image": ""}, {"text": "<p>Instead of worrying about calories, look at your food in terms of color, variety, and\nfreshness. Try to avoid packaged, processed foods. Get some fresh ingredients onto your table and into your lunch bag.\n</p><p>Read the labels. It's important to be aware of what's in your food. Many\npackaged foods claim to be healthy, but they must have large amounts of sugar\nand salt.</p>", "id": 3, "time": "37000", "image": ""}, {"text": "<p>After you eat, stop to consider how you feel. Don't you think that the more you eat\nhealthy food, the better you'll feel after a meal? In time, the junk food you eat\nwill start to make you feel uncomfortable, unsatisfied, and without the energy you need to get through your day.</p><p>Follow these tips and you will create your own schema of healthy eating.", "id": 4, "time": "59000", "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le07ob04re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "_data": [], "type": "video", "template_override": 1}]}]}